# A bytes value carries its capacity and the regime that capacity came from in
# one field, and the in-place append reads both on its hot path. There are
# three regimes and this drives all of them through the same door.
#
#   viewed     a borrowed view. `bytes` of a literal points into the program's
#              own text and owns no buffer, so its capacity is zero and the
#              first append cannot land in place.
#   carried    malloc-backed. The accumulator is threaded through a tail
#              recursion with nothing else in the body, so no beat is
#              bracketed and every growth takes malloc. bytes_malloc counts
#              those buffers and bytes_freed the ones the mutating append
#              released.
#   filled     arena-backed. The outer body allocates a temporary the
#              innermost rewind reclaims, so that loop IS bracketed, and a
#              bytes buffer dying at the rewind is cut from the arena rather
#              than from malloc. bytes_malloc does not count these, which is
#              what tells the two owned regimes apart.
#
# `filled` appends 200 bytes one at a time onto a one-byte seed, which walks
# each arena-backed buffer from its first growth to exactly full and one byte
# past. That boundary is the point of the fixture: a capacity read that adds
# the regime bit to the room instead of masking it off admits one byte more
# than the buffer holds, writes it past the frontier, and moves append_fast
# and append_grow together. Both were watched.
#
# The counters are the pin. append_fast is the store into spare room,
# append_grow the reallocation, bytes_malloc and bytes_freed the malloc
# regime. Flipping the regime bit's polarity moves 900 arena grows into
# bytes_malloc.
import "std/text"

fn carried acc 0
  acc

fn carried acc n
  carried (text/append acc (65 + n % 26)) (n - 1)

fn filled acc 0
  acc

fn filled acc n
  filled (text/append acc (65 + n % 26)) (n - 1)

fn scratched total 0
  total

fn scratched total n
  junk = "k{n % 17}"
  scratch = filled (text/bytes "s") 200
  scratched (total + length scratch + length junk) (n - 1)

pub play =
  viewed = text/append (text/bytes "view") 33
  built = carried (text/bytes "a") 2000
  print "viewed: {text/utf8 viewed}"
  print "carried: {length built}"
  print "scratched: {scratched 0 300}"
